From ee42744d307fd3624ce600fa7b67af629a9299b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 01:46:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00703/11171] [outer-loop] Add pre-push gitlink guard (prevents
 the nano-trm CI/Pages break recurring)

Closes the class of bug behind the 2026-06-06 nano-trm incident (commit
c4c612662): a conductor `git add -A` swallowed a cloned experiment repo as a
submodule gitlink (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules, breaking every GitHub
Actions checkout (Pages, CI, phase1-reproducer) at exit 128.

  - scripts/gitlink_guard.py: refuses pushing to main any tree-mode-160000
    gitlink that lacks a matching .gitmodules entry. Fail-open on git infra
    error, fail-closed on a confirmed stray gitlink. Runs at PUSH time to cover
    the conductor's --no-verify auto-push.
  - scripts/git-hooks/pre-push: now runs BOTH guards (blog-publish + gitlink),
    replaying the captured pre-push stdin to each; non-zero from either blocks.
  - scripts/install-git-hooks.sh: echo updated.
  - ops/known-issues.md: OPERATOR CONSTRAINTS entry + memory
    feedback_no_embedded_repo_gitlinks.

Verified against the real c4c612662 range (blocks, names nano-trm) + clean ranges
(allow) + end-to-end via the installed hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
